{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability: Structure, Budgets, and Reference Limits\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"For frozen tabular classifiers and a fixed empirical probability-scale Shapley game, how do sampled and structure-aware computations compare in single-call reference agreement and repeated-call consistency under finite coalition caps, and what reliability claims remain unsupported?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the evaluated German Credit and ACS income conditions, structure-aware forest attribution and probability-scale logistic integration yield perfectly consistent observed repeated-call top-three sets and signs and high reference agreement, but reference uncertainty, restricted game semantics, and unequal computational access prevent interpreting these results as general deployment reliability or equal-time superiority.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"A bounded computational-reliability study is supported by final per-instance attribution arrays, repeated-call pairs, library comparators, controls, and uncertainty summaries. Four dataset/model conditions test one shared fixed-game thesis, with forest algebra and logistic integration as condition-specific computations. The final evaluation is independently completed and qualified; this is a documented evaluation outcome, not scientific proof of general reliability. A certificate-centered paper is weaker because certificate decisions and acceptance coverage are not recorded. A general high-risk deployment paper exceeds the fixed-background, scalar-encoded, small-instance evidence. A logistic-only paper discards the independently useful forest conditions. A search-success narrative confuses development evidence with the final evaluation. The chosen story retains direct comparisons and limitations without requiring new experiments.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"No edit-mode files, previous_paper directory, or prior manuscript were supplied. Recentered refers to narrowing the broad source-task motivation to the evaluated fixed-game computational question, not to revising an unseen manuscript. Preserving the broad deployment story was rejected; a shared cross-model computation story was selected over a logistic-only recentering.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"There are no staged prior/new manuscript pairs or extra_tasks/aggregated directories; no inherited title, thesis, or figure plan is assumed.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation supplies three final episodes and four public-data/model conditions with one-shot library and split-budget two-start comparators; these observations, not qualitative memory, determine the central results.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.downstream_study and study.* grounding sources are absent. Do not invent a frozen-study selection contract, search-score differences, attempt counts, or an original-incumbent comparison from memory.\\\",\n+    \\\"Recoverable source under results/ideas/03_probability_scale_logistic_shap_by_bounded_fourier_quadrature/program_1/src implements both forest and logistic computations. Earlier reliability.py files differ by the corresponding imports/dispatches, supporting bounded development-set component comparisons rather than a chronology.\\\",\n+    \\\"The best-program manifest links the recoverable implementation to the final-tested configuration at path/selection level. The final manifest records a program-tree digest, but this strategy does not independently establish a byte-for-byte final snapshot match; algorithm descriptions are source-grounded and measured behavior is final-evidence-grounded.\\\",\n+    \\\"VENUE.md and the actual ICLR style require a single-column, anonymized, 8–9 body-page paper; the plan uses readable full-text-width figures rather than assuming a two-column format.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"One-shot library Kernel SHAP\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The evaluator records identity-link shap.KernelExplainer outputs, l1_reg=0.0, for the same frozen model, queries, empirical background, and nominal coalition caps. This is a measured comparator, not a literature-only baseline.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Two-start Kernel SHAP with split coalition caps\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Two independent library estimates each receive half the nominal cap and are averaged. This tests a practical repeat-and-average alternative without silently doubling its coalition allocation; actual row counts and endpoint overhead need not match the one-shot method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Structure-aware fixed-game computation\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"One shared estimator family preserves the finite empirical interventional probability game: exact leaf-literal algebra for forests, bounded Fourier/Owen integration for nonexhaustive logistic requests, exhaustive nonforest computation when the cap covers all subsets, and the existing sampled fallback on numerical rejection. Do not claim observed branch frequencies from unrecorded internal diagnostics.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Sampled path/regression configuration\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The configuration without either structure-aware component has measured development-set outputs. Compare it directly with the forest-enabled configuration on forest conditions; it is not the untouched original incumbent and is not a separately final-evaluated method. Its internal confidence-bound code does not supply measured certificate coverage.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forest-enabled, sampled-logistic configuration\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Its source retains the exact forest branch but lacks logistic quadrature. Matched development episodes isolate the logistic dispatch addition; unchanged forest outputs act as a component-locality check. These comparisons are descriptive selected-development evidence, not independent confirmation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Same-game references and analytic controls\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"ACS has exhaustive 10-feature references; German has the mean of two 4096-coalition library estimates and recorded half-differences, not exact ground truth. Zero, affine, feature-permutation, and reset/replay observations check specific properties but do not validate all nonlinear numerical paths.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary final comparison: normalized L1 reference agreement for the three measured methods at caps 64, 256, and 1024, separately for German/logistic, German/forest, ACS/logistic, and ACS/forest. Preserve episode-level variation and the difference between exhaustive and approximate references.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final reliability decomposition: reference top-three overlap, all-coordinate sign agreement with the evaluator's 1e-8 zero tolerance, and within-instance repeated-call top-three/sign consistency are different quantities. The final aggregate reports reference agreement 0.9975639445869278, top-three overlap 1.0, and sign agreement 0.9997395833333332; no generic reliable/not-reliable label is justified by these alone.\\\",\n+    \\\"Observed candidate repeat-pair top-three and sign agreement is 1.0 in every final empirical condition. Do not infer baseline within-model repeatability: the stored library comparators have one estimate per cap per episode, not six repeated estimates on each frozen model.\\\",\n+    \\\"Reference limitation: near-numerical-precision agreement on exhaustive ACS games contrasts with residual differences against approximate German references. Do not attribute all German residuals to the candidate or all to reference noise. Report the stored reference half-differences separately from confidence intervals.\\\",\n+    \\\"Development-only component comparisons: forest-enabled versus sampled-only on forest conditions, and full structure-aware versus forest-enabled on logistic conditions, at matched caps 64/256 and seeds 1729/2718. Keep these in a clearly labeled development-data results block; never connect configurations as a search trajectory.\\\",\n+    \\\"Negative evidence: splitting cap 64 between two starts has especially low German reference agreement, while high-cap ACS one-shot estimates reach exhaustive computation and close the gap. Show these measured limitations without diagnosing rank deficiency or another cause that the evidence does not identify.\\\",\n+    \\\"Integrity and costs: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true; no failed qualification is reported in this run. Controls, failed-call fraction, efficiency residual, and reset/replay are narrow checks, not an accuracy or validity guarantee. The 700.3707705293782-second final wall total includes multiple methods and reference work and is not candidate latency.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: a fixed empirical game feeds sampled and structure-aware computations; audit repeated-call consistency and same-game reference agreement separately, ending at an explicit deployment-scope boundary.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: a four-panel categorical comparison of final reference agreement by coalition cap and method, with individual episode markers and exact/approximate reference labels; no trajectory lines or search indices.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, component comparison: two panels of matched development-set comparisons for forest algebra and logistic integration, with datasets and caps as categorical conditions and two compared configurations per panel.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"fixed_game_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the fixed-game object, two computational approaches, two distinct reliability assessments, and the limit on deployment interpretation immediately legible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"scientific_role\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; conceptual evidence map with no invented quantitative content\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"fixed game, sampled computation, structure-aware computation, repeat consistency, reference agreement, scope boundary\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The actual ICLR article style sets textwidth=5.5in and textheight=9in and uses one column. Use the full 5.5in text width, approximately 1.6–1.8in high plus a short caption, on page 1 or 2 (about 0.23 body page). Six concise labeled blocks and at least 9pt final-size text remain legible without a miniature algorithm flowchart.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"final_reference_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Compare measured one-shot library, split-cap averaging, and structure-aware outputs within each final dataset/model condition without pooling away reference-quality differences.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"grouped_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"coalition_cap\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized L1 reference agreement = 1/(1 + ||phi-phi_ref||_1/max(||phi_ref||_1,0.001))\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"dataset x classifier, with exhaustive versus approximate reference stated in each panel\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At 5.5in full text width, a 2x2 grid gives approximately 2.6in per panel; three short cap labels and three method series fit with 9pt labels and one shared legend. Target approximately 3.5–4in height plus caption (about 0.48 page). A hypothetical half-width placement would make four panels unreadable. Use a common 0–1 agreement axis and explicit numeric annotations or the companion table for ceiling-level differences, not a concealed truncated scale.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.reference_fidelity\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"component_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Test whether the observed development-data differences localize to the forest and logistic components rather than presenting configuration order as evidence.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"dataset_and_coalition_cap\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized L1 reference agreement, using the same definition as the final comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"forest component and logistic component, explicitly development data\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side panels at 5.5in full text width, approximately 2.2–2.5in high plus caption (about 0.32 page). Each has four abbreviated dataset/cap categories and two configuration series, with the two episode points shown rather than invented standard errors. Keep 9pt labels and explanatory full labels in the caption; simplify rather than shrink. Do not add an ordering axis or arrows between configurations.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"result.top_program_02\\\", \\\"result.top_program_03\\\"]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide substantive implementation, uncertainty, and reproducibility depth after the references while retaining the central final comparisons, component evidence, and decisive scope limitations in the main body; no new experiments or invented posthoc rankings are required.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Fixed-Game Definition and Preprocessing\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the empirical interventional game and probability output scale; document original scalar feature groups, training-only ordinal vocabulary, median imputation and scaling, fixed 16-row background, and fixed query selection using task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/*. Document that this is neither conditional attribution nor raw-preprocessing resampling. Include the actual German and ACS split/provenance records and ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP adapter.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Structure-Aware Computation and Numerical Safeguards\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand forest leaf inclusion/exclusion coefficients, repeated-split intersection, averaging over every background row/tree, and float32 traversal semantics from forest.py. Expand the logistic Fourier/Owen identity, exact inclusion-polynomial quadrature, frequency truncation, refinement checks, work caps, exhaustive dispatch, and sampled fallback from logistic_fourier.py and reliability.py. Explicitly distinguish an analytic frequency-tail bound from an unproved total discretization-error guarantee; validation scripts are available source, not evidence that they were run.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Episode-Level Reliability and Reference Uncertainty\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every stored final case/cap/episode summary, existing case-level instance-bootstrap intervals, analytic-control observations, reset/replay result, reference half-differences, and model fit diagnostics. Explain each interval's conditional scope and keep repetitions, instance pairs, and overlapping episodes from being counted as independent samples. Any extra quantitative panels must be reproducible descriptive views of these arrays, not fabricated confidence bands.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.efficiency_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\", \\\"final.metric.replay_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.failed_fraction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Component Comparison Details\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Supply complete per-condition development comparison tables and the inspected reliability.py dispatch differences. Include unchanged-family checks and any regressions or nonmonotone budget behavior already recorded. Make the development/final separation explicit and do not describe search ranking as an independent replication or report unscored alternatives as measured losses.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"result.top_program_02\\\", \\\"result.top_program_03\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reproducibility and Compute Accounting\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document task/requirements.txt, each retained program_spec.toml, evaluator and dataset provenance files, resource hashes, training and explanation seeds, and offline acquisition/reproduction paths. Distinguish measured total wall time and baseline productive_seconds/prediction_rows from unrecorded candidate per-call latency. List the exact final plot/table scripts once implemented, with source pointers into paper_data.json; do not claim those future scripts already exist. Keep internal machine paths out of the anonymous manuscript.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.wall_seconds\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Successive Improvements\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"certified reliable explanations\\\",\n+    \\\"repeatability proves validity\\\",\n+    \\\"exact German ground truth\\\",\n+    \\\"equal-time superiority\\\",\n+    \\\"safe high-risk deployment\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Main-body architecture and footprint, inclusive of figures/tables: introduction and early overview 1.25 pages; related work 0.65; fixed-game estimand and metrics 1.0; model-specific computation 1.4; experimental and statistical protocol 1.05; results and component comparison 2.0; limitations and interpretation 0.9; conclusion 0.25. Total target 8.5 pages under the supplied 8–9-page venue rule. An 8-page body must fill at least 75% of its final page. Use remaining space for equations, reference limitations and fair comparison, not more search history or oversized figures.\\\",\n+    \\\"Two compact main tables complement the figures: an experimental-design table with dataset version, split, feature count, background, model, reference type and cap; and a final-reliability table with condition-specific reference agreement, stored conditional intervals at their actual scope, top-three/sign agreement and repeat consistency. Keep global integrity checks in a short adjacent paragraph rather than relabeling them as predictive accuracy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Template inspection: .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex uses article plus paper,times; paper.sty specifies 5.5in text width and 9in text height, with no two-column layout. Full_width means one full text column, not a two-column float. Do not use the template's sample title or author block; omit identifying material and final-copy author mode for the double-blind paper while preserving required template infrastructure.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final qualification must remain auditable through final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, and final.qualification.correct. In this run they report completed, qualified, and true. Reader-facing disclosure should say the evaluation met its documented completeness and analytic-control requirements, not that scientific reliability was certified. Review/audit/revision must preserve this scope; if later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, disclose it explicitly and do not diagnose performance, validity or adaptivity causes without criterion evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final tested method is primary. Private-only source bridge: best_program_manifest.json names the recoverable third configuration; final_evaluation independently records final outcomes. No downstream_study or study.* records exist, so do not publish search selection scores, score differences, attempt totals or an alleged original baseline win. The memory-only incumbent score is not a comparator.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.evidence.episodes for the main per-condition results and final.metric.* for aggregate checks. Private-only: result.top_program_01/02/03 identify the full, forest-enabled, and sampled configurations; follow each all_programs evaluation_evidence.episodes array for development comparisons. Those source IDs' scalar values alone do not establish an ablation. Trace the array path and inspected source change in downstream claim mappings; do not invent missing grounding IDs.\\\",\n+    \\\"Data regime: German has 20 supplied scalar feature groups and final retained splits 300 train/100 validation/100 explanation; ACS has 10 groups and 20000/6667/6667. Only the first 16 explanation instances and first 16 training-background rows are used in the final study. These split counts are from the inspected resource records, not measurements of generalization. Name ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP explicitly, retain the provenance adapter and the search/final content-disjointness construction, and do not call it bit-identical historical ACSIncome.\\\",\n+    \\\"Frozen model conditions are logistic regression (lbfgs, max_iter=500, tol=1e-7) and forests (64 trees, max_depth=6, n_jobs=1). Final episode seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; each has caps 64/256/1024 and six candidate calls per cap. Fixed instances recur across episodes; model randomness can differ for forests, while logistic fitting may be deterministic. Do not count these as 48 independent queried people or treat six deterministic repeats as six independent fidelity observations.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use the exact evaluator definitions: reference agreement is reciprocal normalized L1 error with a 0.001 denominator floor; top-three compares absolute attribution sets with original-column tie breaking; sign agreement covers all coordinates with an absolute 1e-8 zero threshold; normalized efficiency residual is capped at one with a 0.001 denominator floor. These are not user-validated reliability thresholds, calibration scores, causal correctness, or fairness assessments.\\\",\n+    \\\"Existing 95% bootstrap intervals resample 16 instance-level agreement summaries after averaging candidate repeats and caps, conditional on one model/reference, with 1000 resamples and seed 84017. They are not per-cap intervals, do not incorporate approximate-reference error, and cannot be averaged into a new interval. Show per-episode points for budget-specific comparisons and label any descriptive range as a range, not a confidence interval. Do not manufacture significance claims.\\\",\n+    \\\"German references average two 4096-coalition library estimates; abs(first-second)/2 is a disagreement proxy, not a confidence bound. ACS references enumerate all 2\"'^10 coalitions. The candidate'\"'s nonforest exhaustive dispatch activates when cap >= 2\"'^d-2, so ACS logistic cap 1024 does not demonstrate the quadrature branch. Forest dispatch precedes that check. Branch acceptance/rejection counts, certificate coverage, and total quadrature error certificates are not recorded; deterministic output does not recover those missing facts.\",\n+    \"Model-agnostic library comparators use prediction queries; the proposed computation receives model parameters. A nominal sampled-coalition cap is not a matched arithmetic, wall-clock or information-access budget. Actual baseline prediction rows are recorded; candidate per-call timing and comparable prediction-cost diagnostics are not. Report measured total time only in its correct all-work scope; do not substitute the source task'\"'s estimated CPU-hour budget for observed usage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Current sources support a bounded engineering/methodology contribution, not first-ever exact tree attribution or first-ever SHAP stability analysis. The bibliography is a noisy retrieved candidate pool with metadata-level provenance, not proof every source has been read. Use only relevant permitted primary works actually consulted and keys present in references.bib, starting from Lundberg2017AUA, Musco2024ProvablyAS, and appropriate tree-attribution records after verification. Missing Owen/empirical-Bernstein/semantics sources cannot be replaced with invented citations or unsupported novelty claims; keep nonessential certificate theory out of the central contribution.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not perform broad reliability-literature discovery or attempt to identify the prohibited paper. No external paper pages were accessed during this strategy stage, and no prohibited encounter was identified here. Do not infer that prior retrieval was fully reviewed or contamination-free merely from its presence. Any actual prohibited encounter must be stopped and recorded with URL and extent of reading.\\\",\n+    \\\"All main quantitative views are descriptive transformations of retained measured arrays, with scripts and source pointers preserved. Do not invent runs, confidence bands, missing measurements, calibration, background-size sensitivity, latency distributions, acceptance coverage, alternative datasets or tested external TreeSHAP/leverage-score baselines. Unscored or unrun alternatives remain missing evidence, never measured losses. Standalone forest/logistic validation scripts being present does not establish their execution.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use vector-first matplotlib outputs: preserve plotting source/data and export both PDF and PNG, PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must prefer PDF whenever it exists. A raster-only full-width figure must be regenerated from source at >=2400px wide, and any column/partial-width raster at >=1200px; never upscale. The concept-figure workflow is orchestrator-owned, uses one editable draw.io overview, and does not itself promise PDF export. Prefer a PDF exported from its vector source when available; otherwise require the full-width raster minimum and a recorded prompt/source manifest. Do not invoke image generation during strategy planning.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use consistent method colors: gray for one-shot library, orange for split-cap averaging, blue for structure-aware computation. Use gray for the disabled component and blue for the enabled component in development comparisons, explicitly label that local contrast, and preserve meanings in legends. Distinguish reference quality with text rather than reassigning method colors. Avoid decorative failure/success icons that imply unmeasured thresholds.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep the main conclusion conditional: one call is adequate for the observed same-game top-three/sign/reference-agreement criteria in these evaluated conditions, not universally adequate as a reason for a prediction. No task-specific acceptable-error threshold or human decision study was prespecified. Small fixed query sets, fixed nonrepresentative background choice, scalar categorical encoding, approximate German references, unrecorded branch diagnostics, and no human/causal/background-shift validation must appear in the main limitations, not only the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"After the main body, flush floats, place references, then clear the page and use appendix plus a Supplementary Information section with substantive subsections. Add a separate LLM Usage section, preferably there, disclosing the documented roles in ideation, code preparation and paper planning/writing without inventing model identifiers or human review. Follow any supplied authoritative appendix rankings later without retroactively changing this strategy or hiding central evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"This is a framing artifact only. Do not create paper.tex or claims_grounding.json here, do not run final-paper validation, and do not claim official-template provenance or submission readiness merely because the supplied local style was inspected. Downstream writing must retain venue anonymization, actual checklist obligations, figure/script traceability, and all evaluation limitations.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy: Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Use the \"'`paper_standalone` family and `write-paper-standalone` skill for a thesis-first ICLR 2026 study. Provisional title: **Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability: Structure, Budgets, and Reference Limits**.\n+\n+**Central question.** For frozen tabular classifiers and a fixed empirical probability-scale Shapley game, how do sampled and structure-aware computations compare in single-call reference agreement and repeated-call consistency under finite coalition caps, and what reliability claims remain unsupported?\n+\n+**Central thesis.** On the evaluated German Credit and ACS income conditions, structure-aware forest attribution and probability-scale logistic integration yield perfectly consistent observed repeated-call top-three sets and signs and high reference agreement, but reference uncertainty, restricted game semantics, and unequal computational access prevent interpreting these results as general deployment reliability or equal-time superiority.\n+\n+This is one shared scientific question with dataset/model-specific adaptations, not separate chronological experiments. The contribution is a bounded computational-reliability comparison and its interpretive limits, not a first-ever exact-tree algorithm, universal reliability theorem, or deployment certification.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification\n+\n+Read final evaluation independently of search and of any proposed downstream-study narrative. Here `paper_data.json.downstream_study` and `study.*` sources are absent. The final qualification sources report:\n+\n+| Grounding source | Reported value |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `final.qualification.status` | `completed` |\n+| `final.qualification.outcome` | `qualified` |\n+| `final.qualification.correct` | `true` |\n+\n+No failed final qualification is reported in this run. This outcome concerns the documented evaluation checks, not proof that explanations are valid reasons for high-risk decisions. Preserve the distinction in writing, review, audit, and revision. If later authoritative evidence reports failure, disclose it and retain its limitations; do not classify its cause as performance, validity, or adaptivity without evaluator diagnostics.\n+\n+Main numerical evidence comes from `final.evidence.episodes`. Final aggregates include reference agreement **0.9975639445869278**, reference top-three overlap **1.0**, and all-coordinate sign agreement **0.9997395833333332**, grounded in their corresponding `final.metric.*` sources. Candidate repeat-pair top-three and sign agreement are **1.0** throughout the retained final empirical observations. These are separate findings, not one undifferentiated reliability score. Controls, efficiency, failed-call fraction and replay are narrow checks.\n+\n+The final wall total, **700.3707705293782 seconds**, covers the evaluation workload, including references and comparators; it is not per-explanation latency or a candidate-only runtime. The source brief'\"'s CPU-hour estimate is not measured usage.\n+\n+### What is actually evaluated\n+\n+- German Credit and **ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP**, each with logistic regression and random forests: four conditions under one thesis.\n+- Final episode seeds: **104729, 130363, 155921**; coalition caps **64, 256, 1024**; **six** candidate calls per cap; **16** fixed query instances and **16** fixed training-background rows per condition.\n+- German has **20** scalar feature groups and retained final splits **300/100/100** for training/validation/explanation. ACS has **10** groups and **20000/6667/6667**. Split counts are inspected resource provenance, not generalization measurements.\n+- Preprocessing is training-fitted ordinal categorical encoding, numeric median imputation, and standardization of supplied original groups. This is not arbitrary raw-data masking or a one-hot-grouping experiment.\n+- Logistic regression uses \"'`lbfgs`, `max_iter=500`, `tol=1e-7`; forests have **64** trees, maximum depth **6**, and `n_jobs=1`.\n+- ACS references enumerate the finite **10**-feature game. German references average two **4096**-coalition library estimates; their half-difference is a recorded disagreement proxy, not a confidence interval or exact ground truth.\n+\n+These settings are traceable to the final episode arrays, `task/evaluate_final.py`, and `task/resources/final/`. The ACS relationship-field adapter and search/final predictor-content separation must remain explicit. Do not call the adapted task bit-identical historical ACSIncome.\n+\n+## Framing Choice and Alternatives\n+\n+**Story status: recentered.** There is no prior manuscript, edit-context file, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` directory. This decision narrows the broad source-task motivation rather than modifying an unseen prior paper.\n+\n+| Candidate story | Decision and grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Preserve the broad claim about reliable reasons in high-risk deployment | Reject: no human decision evidence, causal validation, conditional-game study, or background-shift evaluation. |\n+| Shared fixed-game computation across model families | Select: both forest and logistic conditions have measured comparators and reference evidence, with inspectable component changes. |\n+| Recenter solely on logistic quadrature | Reject as primary: discards useful forest evidence; no recorded branch coverage or total quadrature-error certificate supports making quadrature alone the whole claim. |\n+| Center single-call confidence certificates | Reject: certificate decisions and acceptance coverage were not persisted; implementation presence is not measured utility. |\n+| Narrate the selected search result | Reject: discovery order and selection scores do not answer the scientific question or establish final performance. |\n+\n+The recoverable full implementation is under `results/ideas/03_probability_scale_logistic_shap_by_bounded_fourier_quadrature/program_1/src/`. The best-program manifest links this configuration to the final-tested method at selection/path level; the final program-tree digest is recorded but has not independently been matched to a recovered byte-identical final snapshot in this stage. Describe source-grounded mechanisms and evidence-grounded behavior separately.\n+\n+Private-only selection context must not leak into manuscript labels. Without `study.*`, do not manufacture a frozen-study selection contract, publish search score differences or attempt totals, or use the memory-only original-incumbent score as a comparison. The stored library comparators remain valid measured baselines.\n+\n+## Methods Worth Including\n+\n+1. **One-shot library Kernel SHAP — baseline.** Same model, empirical background, queries, identity link and nominal cap; `l1_reg=0.0`.\n+2. **Two-start split-cap Kernel SHAP — baseline.** Average two independent half-cap estimates. Explain that endpoint overhead and actual prediction rows need not match one-shot cost.\n+3. **Structure-aware fixed-game computation — proposed family.** Exact forest leaf-literal algebra and probability-scale logistic Fourier/Owen integration, with exhaustive nonforest dispatch when all subsets fit and the existing sampled fallback on numerical rejection. Explain the common estimand before model-specific computations.\n+4. **Sampled path/regression configuration — development ablation.** Compared with the forest-enabled configuration on forest conditions; not the untouched original incumbent.\n+5. **Forest-enabled, sampled-logistic configuration — development ablation.** Compared with the full family on logistic conditions; unchanged forest behavior checks component locality.\n+6. **Same-game references and analytic controls — supporting evidence.** Exhaustive ACS, approximate German, zero/affine/permutation controls, and reset/replay. Do not count them as extra public datasets or as full nonlinear validation.\n+\n+Inspection of `reliability.py` confirms that the forest comparison adds its import/dispatch and the logistic comparison adds its import/dispatch. Stored matched development episodes support direct component contrasts at seeds **1729/2718** and caps **64/256**. Label these comparisons development data throughout; they are neither final holdout ablations nor independent confirmations. Complete tables may go in the supplement, but the main component comparison must remain visible.\n+\n+Do not expand the paper into unmeasured neural models, background resampling, alternative certificates, leverage-score methods, external TreeSHAP implementations, or additional datasets. Relevant literature methods may be context, not measured baselines.\n+\n+## Results Organization and Statistical Meaning\n+\n+### Main final comparison\n+\n+Compare three methods at each cap in each dataset/model condition. Use normalized L1 **reference agreement**:\n+\n+`1 / (1 + ||phi - phi_ref||_1 / max(||phi_ref||_1, 0.001))`.\n+\n+Show individual episode markers rather than invented per-cap confidence bands. Preserve the distinction between approximate German and exhaustive ACS references. High-cap ACS one-shot computation can close the gap; split-cap averaging has particularly poor German agreement at cap 64. Report these negative and boundary results without an unsupported diagnosis such as regression rank failure.\n+\n+### Distinct reliability assessments\n+\n+- Reference top-three overlap uses absolute values and original-column tie breaking.\n+- Reference sign agreement covers **all coordinates**, with absolute zero tolerance **1e-8**; it is not signed-top-three accuracy.\n+- Repeated-call top-three and sign agreement compare candidate outputs on the same fixed game. Baseline outputs do not include six within-model repetitions, so a matching baseline repeatability comparison is unavailable.\n+- Normalized efficiency residual uses a **0.001** denominator floor and is capped at one. It is not reference fidelity.\n+\n+Existing case-level 95% bootstrap intervals first average candidate agreement over repetitions and caps and then resample **16 instances**, using **1000** bootstrap draws and seed **84017**. They condition on a fitted model and its reference; they are not per-cap intervals and omit reference-estimation uncertainty. Do not average interval endpoints into a new interval. The same instances recur across episodes, and fitted forests may differ with seeds; neither repeated calls nor overlapping episode samples create independent people. Near-degenerate intervals from deterministic outputs do not imply negligible deployment uncertainty.\n+\n+### Limits required beside the main results\n+\n+Residual German differences cannot be assigned solely to reference noise or solely to candidate error. Deterministic outputs cannot establish the active internal branch. Nonforest exhaustive dispatch occurs at cap `>= 2''^d - 2`; ACS logistic cap 1024 is therefore not evidence of the quadrature branch. Internal certificate acceptance/rejection, quadrature rejection frequency, candidate per-call runtime, and total discretization-error guarantees are unavailable.\n+\n+The proposed family has model-parameter access; library methods use prediction queries. A nominal sampled-coalition cap does not equate arithmetic work, information access, or wall time. Do not claim equal-time superiority. The quadrature'\"'s analytic frequency-tail bound does not bound all discretization error; refinement agreement and efficiency are numerical diagnostics. Independent validation scripts are present but their preparation records say they were not run. Their presence cannot become a validation result.\n+\n+No acceptable-error or user-decision reliability threshold was prespecified. State that one call meets the **observed same-game criteria in these retained conditions**, not that a universal trustworthy-explanation threshold was established.\n+\n+## Figure Specifications and Layout\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`article` and `paper,times`; `paper.sty` sets **5.5 inches text width**, **9 inches text height**, and a **single-column** layout. Full width means that one text column, not a two-column float. Half-width placement is not appropriate for the required composites.\n+\n+### Figure 1 — `fixed_game_overview`\n+\n+- **Required; diagram; generator `generate-concept-figure`.** Early placement on page 1 or 2.\n+- One panel with at most six concise blocks: fixed game, sampled computation, structure-aware computation, repeat consistency, reference agreement, and scope boundary. Explain details in the caption rather than adding microtext.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **1.6–1.8 inches** high plus caption; intended footprint about **0.23 page**. At least **9-point** final-size text.\n+- Budget: **1 panel**, **1 per row**, **6 main categories/blocks**, **2 computational branches**. No invented numeric annotations or causal/deployment guarantees.\n+- Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes` plus the inspected estimator source. This is an evidence map, not a claim that a confidence certificate was observed.\n+- Use the orchestrator-owned editable draw.io concept-figure workflow later; do not run it during strategy planning. At most this one overview uses that generator.\n+\n+### Figure 2 — `final_reference_comparison`\n+\n+- **Required; grouped categorical dot plot; matplotlib.** Four dataset/model panels in a **2x2** arrangement.\n+- Three cap categories and three method series per panel; per-episode points, one shared legend, explicit exhaustive/approximate reference labels. A common **0–1** agreement scale keeps the low split-cap outcomes visible; communicate near-ceiling differences through concise values or the companion table, not a hidden truncated scale.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **3.5–4 inches** high plus caption; footprint about **0.48 page**. Roughly **2.6 inches** per panel supports short cap labels and at least **9-point** text.\n+- Budget: **4 panels**, **2 per row**, **3 categories**, **3 series**. No search-order lines or per-cap error bars borrowed from budget-pooled intervals.\n+- Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.reference_fidelity`.\n+\n+### Figure 3 — `component_comparison`\n+\n+- **Required; paired categorical dot comparison; matplotlib.** Two panels: forest component and logistic component.\n+- Four dataset/cap categories per panel, two compared configurations, and the two matched development episode points. Show the relevant disabled/enabled contrast rather than all configurations in an ordered sequence.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **2.2–2.5 inches** high plus caption; footprint about **0.32 page**. Short labels and at least **9-point** text are required; simplify instead of shrinking.\n+- Budget: **2 panels**, **2 per row**, **4 categories**, **2 series**. Explicitly mark development data. No campaign progression, ranking, or final-set ablation claim.\n+- Private grounding bridge: `result.top_program_03` identifies sampled-only, `result.top_program_02` forest-enabled, and `result.top_program_01` full computation. Use their actual `all_programs[*].evaluation_evidence.episodes` arrays and inspected source changes, not the scalar selection scores, as evidence for the plotted component contrasts.\n+\n+### Export and consistency contract\n+\n+Quantitative figures must retain source/data and export **PDF plus PNG**, PNG at **300 DPI**. LaTeX must use the PDF whenever available. For raster-only full-width assets, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide**; column/partial-width raster assets require **at least 1200 pixels**. Never upscale an existing raster. The concept workflow does not itself promise a PDF: prefer one exported from its editable vector source when available, otherwise meet the raster minimum and preserve the prompt/source manifest.\n+\n+Use gray for one-shot library, orange for split-cap averaging, and blue for structure-aware computation. Component plots may use gray/blue for the explicitly labeled disabled/enabled contrast. Keep reference quality as text labels, not a remapping of method colors. No trajectory figures are warranted.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Reader Value\n+\n+Target **8.5 body pages** under the supplied **8–9-page** brief. Figures and tables are already included in these allocations:\n+\n+| Material | Planned pages |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Introduction and early overview | 1.25 |\n+| Related work | 0.65 |\n+| Fixed-game estimand and metrics | 1.00 |\n+| Model-specific computation | 1.40 |\n+| Experimental and statistical protocol | 1.05 |\n+| Results and component comparison | 2.00 |\n+| Limitations and interpretation | 0.90 |\n+| Conclusion | 0.25 |\n+\n+Keep two compact main tables: experimental geometry and condition-specific final reliability. The latter can present the existing conditional intervals at their true scope, alongside separate repeat consistency, reference top-three/sign agreement, and a nearby integrity-check paragraph. Do not force all diagnostics into an unreadable table.\n+\n+Spend available space on the common game definition, the nonlinear probability-scale mechanism, independent meaning of metrics, reference limitations, and fair-compute discussion. Do not pad with method history, oversized graphics, redundant tables, untested possibilities, or search scores. If ending at eight pages, its last page must be at least 75% filled; do not alter margins or shrink type to manipulate this. The supplied template'\"'s sample final-copy author block is not suitable for double-blind submission.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Flush main floats, place references, then clear the page, enter appendix mode, and add **Supplementary Information**. The following substantive sections use available evidence; they do not require new experiments or guessed posthoc rankings:\n+\n+1. **Fixed-Game Definition and Preprocessing.** Expand the estimand, original-group representation, training-only preprocessing, exact data/split provenance and ACS adapter. Sources: \"'`final.evidence.episodes` with inspected `task/evaluate_final.py` and final resource records.\n+2. **Structure-Aware Computation and Numerical Safeguards.** Include leaf inclusion/exclusion coefficients, repeated splits and float semantics, Fourier/Owen integration, inclusion quadrature, frequency-tail versus discretization distinction, dispatch and fallback. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `result.top_program_01`, and the recoverable estimator files; label unrun validation scripts accurately.\n+3. **Episode-Level Reliability and Reference Uncertainty.** Complete per-case/cap/episode tables, stored bootstrap intervals at their actual scope, reference half-differences, model diagnostics, controls and replay. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes` and `final.metric.efficiency_error`, `final.metric.control_pass_rate`, `final.metric.replay_error`, `final.metric.failed_fraction`.\n+4. **Component Comparison Details.** Full development comparison tables, source dispatch differences, unchanged-family checks, and recorded regressions/nonmonotone cap behavior. Sources: `result.top_program_01`, `result.top_program_02`, `result.top_program_03` followed to their episode arrays. No selection-score narrative or final-confirmation claim.\n+5. **Reproducibility and Compute Accounting.** Dependencies, program specifications, seeds, offline data acquisition/provenance, hashes, commands, measured timing scopes, and exact figure/table script mapping once implemented. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.wall_seconds`, and the three final qualification sources, with inspected local specifications/resources. No identifying internal paths in the anonymous submission.\n+\n+Add a separate **LLM Usage** section, preferably after these appendix subsections, describing documented ideation, code-preparation, framing and writing roles precisely. Do not invent model identifiers, human verification, or independent execution. Follow later authoritative appendix rankings without retroactively rewriting this strategy; never move essential final evidence or decisive limitations out of the body.\n+\n+## Literature, Access, and Disclosure Boundaries\n+\n+The existing bibliography is a noisy retrieved candidate pool with metadata-level provenance. It is not evidence that every source was read. Start only with relevant permitted primary records such as `Lundberg2017AUA`, `Musco2024ProvablyAS`, and appropriate tree-attribution records after actual source verification. Do not use irrelevant retrievals as citation padding, invent missing Owen/empirical-Bernstein/semantic references, or claim unverified theoretical novelty. Nonessential certificate theory should not carry the central thesis.\n+\n+No external paper pages were accessed in this strategy stage and no prohibited encounter was identified here. This does not certify earlier retrieval as reviewed or contamination-free. Do not attempt to identify the prohibited study or conduct broad rerun-reliability discovery. Stop and record any actual forbidden encounter, including where it occurred and how much was read.\n+\n+## Anti-Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Avoid headings **Search Progression**, **Campaign Phases**, **Milestones**, **First Valid Result**, **Iteration History**, **Experiment A / Experiment B**, **Winning Configuration**, and **Successive Improvements**.\n+\n+Forbidden visible wording includes “we then tried,” “subsequent improvements,” “first valid result,” “next-best,” “later variants,” and the internal labels listed in the JSON contract. Also avoid “state of the art,” “certified reliable explanations,” “repeatability proves validity,” “exact German ground truth,” “equal-time superiority,” and “safe high-risk deployment.” Private-only source identifiers in this memo are not recommended manuscript terminology.\n+\n+Never turn unscored or unrun alternatives into measured losses. Never invent significance, certificate coverage, quadrature branch counts, candidate latency, robustness studies, additional datasets or external-baseline experiments. Retain the fixed small query set, fixed background, scalar encoding, approximate German reference, missing branch diagnostics, and absent human/causal/background-shift validation in the main limitations.\n+\n+This stage produces strategy only: no `paper.tex`, no `claims_grounding.json`, no final-paper validation, and no claim of submission readiness or verified official-template provenance merely from inspecting the supplied local style.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'apply_patch() { codex --codex-run-as-apply-patch \"$(cat)\"; }\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability: Structure, Budgets, and Reference Limits\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"For frozen tabular classifiers and a fixed empirical probability-scale Shapley game, how do sampled and structure-aware computations compare in single-call reference agreement and repeated-call consistency under finite coalition caps, and what reliability claims remain unsupported?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the evaluated German Credit and ACS income conditions, structure-aware forest attribution and probability-scale logistic integration yield perfectly consistent observed repeated-call top-three sets and signs and high reference agreement, but reference uncertainty, restricted game semantics, and unequal computational access prevent interpreting these results as general deployment reliability or equal-time superiority.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"A bounded computational-reliability study is supported by final per-instance attribution arrays, repeated-call pairs, library comparators, controls, and uncertainty summaries. Four dataset/model conditions test one shared fixed-game thesis, with forest algebra and logistic integration as condition-specific computations. The final evaluation is independently completed and qualified; this is a documented evaluation outcome, not scientific proof of general reliability. A certificate-centered paper is weaker because certificate decisions and acceptance coverage are not recorded. A general high-risk deployment paper exceeds the fixed-background, scalar-encoded, small-instance evidence. A logistic-only paper discards the independently useful forest conditions. A search-success narrative confuses development evidence with the final evaluation. The chosen story retains direct comparisons and limitations without requiring new experiments.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"recentered\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"No edit-mode files, previous_paper directory, or prior manuscript were supplied. Recentered refers to narrowing the broad source-task motivation to the evaluated fixed-game computational question, not to revising an unseen manuscript. Preserving the broad deployment story was rejected; a shared cross-model computation story was selected over a logistic-only recentering.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"There are no staged prior/new manuscript pairs or extra_tasks/aggregated directories; no inherited title, thesis, or figure plan is assumed.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation supplies three final episodes and four public-data/model conditions with one-shot library and split-budget two-start comparators; these observations, not qualitative memory, determine the central results.\\\",\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.downstream_study and study.* grounding sources are absent. Do not invent a frozen-study selection contract, search-score differences, attempt counts, or an original-incumbent comparison from memory.\\\",\n+    \\\"Recoverable source under results/ideas/03_probability_scale_logistic_shap_by_bounded_fourier_quadrature/program_1/src implements both forest and logistic computations. Earlier reliability.py files differ by the corresponding imports/dispatches, supporting bounded development-set component comparisons rather than a chronology.\\\",\n+    \\\"The best-program manifest links the recoverable implementation to the final-tested configuration at path/selection level. The final manifest records a program-tree digest, but this strategy does not independently establish a byte-for-byte final snapshot match; algorithm descriptions are source-grounded and measured behavior is final-evidence-grounded.\\\",\n+    \\\"VENUE.md and the actual ICLR style require a single-column, anonymized, 8–9 body-page paper; the plan uses readable full-text-width figures rather than assuming a two-column format.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"One-shot library Kernel SHAP\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The evaluator records identity-link shap.KernelExplainer outputs, l1_reg=0.0, for the same frozen model, queries, empirical background, and nominal coalition caps. This is a measured comparator, not a literature-only baseline.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Two-start Kernel SHAP with split coalition caps\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Two independent library estimates each receive half the nominal cap and are averaged. This tests a practical repeat-and-average alternative without silently doubling its coalition allocation; actual row counts and endpoint overhead need not match the one-shot method.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Structure-aware fixed-game computation\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"One shared estimator family preserves the finite empirical interventional probability game: exact leaf-literal algebra for forests, bounded Fourier/Owen integration for nonexhaustive logistic requests, exhaustive nonforest computation when the cap covers all subsets, and the existing sampled fallback on numerical rejection. Do not claim observed branch frequencies from unrecorded internal diagnostics.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Sampled path/regression configuration\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The configuration without either structure-aware component has measured development-set outputs. Compare it directly with the forest-enabled configuration on forest conditions; it is not the untouched original incumbent and is not a separately final-evaluated method. Its internal confidence-bound code does not supply measured certificate coverage.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forest-enabled, sampled-logistic configuration\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"ablation\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Its source retains the exact forest branch but lacks logistic quadrature. Matched development episodes isolate the logistic dispatch addition; unchanged forest outputs act as a component-locality check. These comparisons are descriptive selected-development evidence, not independent confirmation.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Same-game references and analytic controls\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"ACS has exhaustive 10-feature references; German has the mean of two 4096-coalition library estimates and recorded half-differences, not exact ground truth. Zero, affine, feature-permutation, and reset/replay observations check specific properties but do not validate all nonlinear numerical paths.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary final comparison: normalized L1 reference agreement for the three measured methods at caps 64, 256, and 1024, separately for German/logistic, German/forest, ACS/logistic, and ACS/forest. Preserve episode-level variation and the difference between exhaustive and approximate references.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final reliability decomposition: reference top-three overlap, all-coordinate sign agreement with the evaluator's 1e-8 zero tolerance, and within-instance repeated-call top-three/sign consistency are different quantities. The final aggregate reports reference agreement 0.9975639445869278, top-three overlap 1.0, and sign agreement 0.9997395833333332; no generic reliable/not-reliable label is justified by these alone.\\\",\n+    \\\"Observed candidate repeat-pair top-three and sign agreement is 1.0 in every final empirical condition. Do not infer baseline within-model repeatability: the stored library comparators have one estimate per cap per episode, not six repeated estimates on each frozen model.\\\",\n+    \\\"Reference limitation: near-numerical-precision agreement on exhaustive ACS games contrasts with residual differences against approximate German references. Do not attribute all German residuals to the candidate or all to reference noise. Report the stored reference half-differences separately from confidence intervals.\\\",\n+    \\\"Development-only component comparisons: forest-enabled versus sampled-only on forest conditions, and full structure-aware versus forest-enabled on logistic conditions, at matched caps 64/256 and seeds 1729/2718. Keep these in a clearly labeled development-data results block; never connect configurations as a search trajectory.\\\",\n+    \\\"Negative evidence: splitting cap 64 between two starts has especially low German reference agreement, while high-cap ACS one-shot estimates reach exhaustive computation and close the gap. Show these measured limitations without diagnosing rank deficiency or another cause that the evidence does not identify.\\\",\n+    \\\"Integrity and costs: final.qualification.status=completed, final.qualification.outcome=qualified, final.qualification.correct=true; no failed qualification is reported in this run. Controls, failed-call fraction, efficiency residual, and reset/replay are narrow checks, not an accuracy or validity guarantee. The 700.3707705293782-second final wall total includes multiple methods and reference work and is not candidate latency.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Figure 1, early overview: a fixed empirical game feeds sampled and structure-aware computations; audit repeated-call consistency and same-game reference agreement separately, ending at an explicit deployment-scope boundary.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 2, main comparison: a four-panel categorical comparison of final reference agreement by coalition cap and method, with individual episode markers and exact/approximate reference labels; no trajectory lines or search indices.\\\",\n+    \\\"Figure 3, component comparison: two panels of matched development-set comparisons for forest algebra and logistic integration, with datasets and caps as categorical conditions and two compared configurations per panel.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"fixed_game_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Make the fixed-game object, two computational approaches, two distinct reliability assessments, and the limit on deployment interpretation immediately legible.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"scientific_role\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; conceptual evidence map with no invented quantitative content\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"fixed game, sampled computation, structure-aware computation, repeat consistency, reference agreement, scope boundary\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"The actual ICLR article style sets textwidth=5.5in and textheight=9in and uses one column. Use the full 5.5in text width, approximately 1.6–1.8in high plus a short caption, on page 1 or 2 (about 0.23 body page). Six concise labeled blocks and at least 9pt final-size text remain legible without a miniature algorithm flowchart.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"final_reference_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Compare measured one-shot library, split-cap averaging, and structure-aware outputs within each final dataset/model condition without pooling away reference-quality differences.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"grouped_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"coalition_cap\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized L1 reference agreement = 1/(1 + ||phi-phi_ref||_1/max(||phi_ref||_1,0.001))\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"dataset x classifier, with exhaustive versus approximate reference stated in each panel\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At 5.5in full text width, a 2x2 grid gives approximately 2.6in per panel; three short cap labels and three method series fit with 9pt labels and one shared legend. Target approximately 3.5–4in height plus caption (about 0.48 page). A hypothetical half-width placement would make four panels unreadable. Use a common 0–1 agreement axis and explicit numeric annotations or the companion table for ceiling-level differences, not a concealed truncated scale.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.reference_fidelity\\\"]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"component_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Test whether the observed development-data differences localize to the forest and logistic components rather than presenting configuration order as evidence.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"paired_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"dataset_and_coalition_cap\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"normalized L1 reference agreement, using the same definition as the final comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"forest component and logistic component, explicitly development data\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Two side-by-side panels at 5.5in full text width, approximately 2.2–2.5in high plus caption (about 0.32 page). Each has four abbreviated dataset/cap categories and two configuration series, with the two episode points shown rather than invented standard errors. Keep 9pt labels and explanatory full labels in the caption; simplify rather than shrink. Do not add an ordering axis or arrows between configurations.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"min_rendered_font_pt\\\": 9,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"result.top_program_02\\\", \\\"result.top_program_03\\\"]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Provide substantive implementation, uncertainty, and reproducibility depth after the references while retaining the central final comparisons, component evidence, and decisive scope limitations in the main body; no new experiments or invented posthoc rankings are required.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Fixed-Game Definition and Preprocessing\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand the empirical interventional game and probability output scale; document original scalar feature groups, training-only ordinal vocabulary, median imputation and scaling, fixed 16-row background, and fixed query selection using task/evaluate_final.py and task/resources/final/*. Document that this is neither conditional attribution nor raw-preprocessing resampling. Include the actual German and ACS split/provenance records and ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP adapter.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Structure-Aware Computation and Numerical Safeguards\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Expand forest leaf inclusion/exclusion coefficients, repeated-split intersection, averaging over every background row/tree, and float32 traversal semantics from forest.py. Expand the logistic Fourier/Owen identity, exact inclusion-polynomial quadrature, frequency truncation, refinement checks, work caps, exhaustive dispatch, and sampled fallback from logistic_fourier.py and reliability.py. Explicitly distinguish an analytic frequency-tail bound from an unproved total discretization-error guarantee; validation scripts are available source, not evidence that they were run.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"result.top_program_01\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Episode-Level Reliability and Reference Uncertainty\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tabulate every stored final case/cap/episode summary, existing case-level instance-bootstrap intervals, analytic-control observations, reset/replay result, reference half-differences, and model fit diagnostics. Explain each interval's conditional scope and keep repetitions, instance pairs, and overlapping episodes from being counted as independent samples. Any extra quantitative panels must be reproducible descriptive views of these arrays, not fabricated confidence bands.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.efficiency_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_pass_rate\\\", \\\"final.metric.replay_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.failed_fraction\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Component Comparison Details\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Supply complete per-condition development comparison tables and the inspected reliability.py dispatch differences. Include unchanged-family checks and any regressions or nonmonotone budget behavior already recorded. Make the development/final separation explicit and do not describe search ranking as an independent replication or report unscored alternatives as measured losses.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"result.top_program_02\\\", \\\"result.top_program_03\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Reproducibility and Compute Accounting\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document task/requirements.txt, each retained program_spec.toml, evaluator and dataset provenance files, resource hashes, training and explanation seeds, and offline acquisition/reproduction paths. Distinguish measured total wall time and baseline productive_seconds/prediction_rows from unrecorded candidate per-call latency. List the exact final plot/table scripts once implemented, with source pointers into paper_data.json; do not claim those future scripts already exist. Keep internal machine paths out of the anonymous manuscript.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.wall_seconds\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Phases\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Iteration History\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Winning Configuration\\\",\n+    \\\"Successive Improvements\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"state of the art\\\",\n+    \\\"certified reliable explanations\\\",\n+    \\\"repeatability proves validity\\\",\n+    \\\"exact German ground truth\\\",\n+    \\\"equal-time superiority\\\",\n+    \\\"safe high-risk deployment\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Main-body architecture and footprint, inclusive of figures/tables: introduction and early overview 1.25 pages; related work 0.65; fixed-game estimand and metrics 1.0; model-specific computation 1.4; experimental and statistical protocol 1.05; results and component comparison 2.0; limitations and interpretation 0.9; conclusion 0.25. Total target 8.5 pages under the supplied 8–9-page venue rule. An 8-page body must fill at least 75% of its final page. Use remaining space for equations, reference limitations and fair comparison, not more search history or oversized figures.\\\",\n+    \\\"Two compact main tables complement the figures: an experimental-design table with dataset version, split, feature count, background, model, reference type and cap; and a final-reliability table with condition-specific reference agreement, stored conditional intervals at their actual scope, top-three/sign agreement and repeat consistency. Keep global integrity checks in a short adjacent paragraph rather than relabeling them as predictive accuracy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Template inspection: .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex uses article plus paper,times; paper.sty specifies 5.5in text width and 9in text height, with no two-column layout. Full_width means one full text column, not a two-column float. Do not use the template's sample title or author block; omit identifying material and final-copy author mode for the double-blind paper while preserving required template infrastructure.\\\",\n+    \\\"Final qualification must remain auditable through final.qualification.status, final.qualification.outcome, and final.qualification.correct. In this run they report completed, qualified, and true. Reader-facing disclosure should say the evaluation met its documented completeness and analytic-control requirements, not that scientific reliability was certified. Review/audit/revision must preserve this scope; if later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, disclose it explicitly and do not diagnose performance, validity or adaptivity causes without criterion evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final tested method is primary. Private-only source bridge: best_program_manifest.json names the recoverable third configuration; final_evaluation independently records final outcomes. No downstream_study or study.* records exist, so do not publish search selection scores, score differences, attempt totals or an alleged original baseline win. The memory-only incumbent score is not a comparator.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.evidence.episodes for the main per-condition results and final.metric.* for aggregate checks. Private-only: result.top_program_01/02/03 identify the full, forest-enabled, and sampled configurations; follow each all_programs evaluation_evidence.episodes array for development comparisons. Those source IDs' scalar values alone do not establish an ablation. Trace the array path and inspected source change in downstream claim mappings; do not invent missing grounding IDs.\\\",\n+    \\\"Data regime: German has 20 supplied scalar feature groups and final retained splits 300 train/100 validation/100 explanation; ACS has 10 groups and 20000/6667/6667. Only the first 16 explanation instances and first 16 training-background rows are used in the final study. These split counts are from the inspected resource records, not measurements of generalization. Name ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP explicitly, retain the provenance adapter and the search/final content-disjointness construction, and do not call it bit-identical historical ACSIncome.\\\",\n+    \\\"Frozen model conditions are logistic regression (lbfgs, max_iter=500, tol=1e-7) and forests (64 trees, max_depth=6, n_jobs=1). Final episode seeds are 104729, 130363 and 155921; each has caps 64/256/1024 and six candidate calls per cap. Fixed instances recur across episodes; model randomness can differ for forests, while logistic fitting may be deterministic. Do not count these as 48 independent queried people or treat six deterministic repeats as six independent fidelity observations.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use the exact evaluator definitions: reference agreement is reciprocal normalized L1 error with a 0.001 denominator floor; top-three compares absolute attribution sets with original-column tie breaking; sign agreement covers all coordinates with an absolute 1e-8 zero threshold; normalized efficiency residual is capped at one with a 0.001 denominator floor. These are not user-validated reliability thresholds, calibration scores, causal correctness, or fairness assessments.\\\",\n+    \\\"Existing 95% bootstrap intervals resample 16 instance-level agreement summaries after averaging candidate repeats and caps, conditional on one model/reference, with 1000 resamples and seed 84017. They are not per-cap intervals, do not incorporate approximate-reference error, and cannot be averaged into a new interval. Show per-episode points for budget-specific comparisons and label any descriptive range as a range, not a confidence interval. Do not manufacture significance claims.\\\",\n+    \\\"German references average two 4096-coalition library estimates; abs(first-second)/2 is a disagreement proxy, not a confidence bound. ACS references enumerate all 2\"'^10 coalitions. The candidate'\"'s nonforest exhaustive dispatch activates when cap >= 2\"'^d-2, so ACS logistic cap 1024 does not demonstrate the quadrature branch. Forest dispatch precedes that check. Branch acceptance/rejection counts, certificate coverage, and total quadrature error certificates are not recorded; deterministic output does not recover those missing facts.\",\n+    \"Model-agnostic library comparators use prediction queries; the proposed computation receives model parameters. A nominal sampled-coalition cap is not a matched arithmetic, wall-clock or information-access budget. Actual baseline prediction rows are recorded; candidate per-call timing and comparable prediction-cost diagnostics are not. Report measured total time only in its correct all-work scope; do not substitute the source task'\"'s estimated CPU-hour budget for observed usage.\\\",\n+    \\\"Current sources support a bounded engineering/methodology contribution, not first-ever exact tree attribution or first-ever SHAP stability analysis. The bibliography is a noisy retrieved candidate pool with metadata-level provenance, not proof every source has been read. Use only relevant permitted primary works actually consulted and keys present in references.bib, starting from Lundberg2017AUA, Musco2024ProvablyAS, and appropriate tree-attribution records after verification. Missing Owen/empirical-Bernstein/semantics sources cannot be replaced with invented citations or unsupported novelty claims; keep nonessential certificate theory out of the central contribution.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not perform broad reliability-literature discovery or attempt to identify the prohibited paper. No external paper pages were accessed during this strategy stage, and no prohibited encounter was identified here. Do not infer that prior retrieval was fully reviewed or contamination-free merely from its presence. Any actual prohibited encounter must be stopped and recorded with URL and extent of reading.\\\",\n+    \\\"All main quantitative views are descriptive transformations of retained measured arrays, with scripts and source pointers preserved. Do not invent runs, confidence bands, missing measurements, calibration, background-size sensitivity, latency distributions, acceptance coverage, alternative datasets or tested external TreeSHAP/leverage-score baselines. Unscored or unrun alternatives remain missing evidence, never measured losses. Standalone forest/logistic validation scripts being present does not establish their execution.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use vector-first matplotlib outputs: preserve plotting source/data and export both PDF and PNG, PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must prefer PDF whenever it exists. A raster-only full-width figure must be regenerated from source at >=2400px wide, and any column/partial-width raster at >=1200px; never upscale. The concept-figure workflow is orchestrator-owned, uses one editable draw.io overview, and does not itself promise PDF export. Prefer a PDF exported from its vector source when available; otherwise require the full-width raster minimum and a recorded prompt/source manifest. Do not invoke image generation during strategy planning.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use consistent method colors: gray for one-shot library, orange for split-cap averaging, blue for structure-aware computation. Use gray for the disabled component and blue for the enabled component in development comparisons, explicitly label that local contrast, and preserve meanings in legends. Distinguish reference quality with text rather than reassigning method colors. Avoid decorative failure/success icons that imply unmeasured thresholds.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep the main conclusion conditional: one call is adequate for the observed same-game top-three/sign/reference-agreement criteria in these evaluated conditions, not universally adequate as a reason for a prediction. No task-specific acceptable-error threshold or human decision study was prespecified. Small fixed query sets, fixed nonrepresentative background choice, scalar categorical encoding, approximate German references, unrecorded branch diagnostics, and no human/causal/background-shift validation must appear in the main limitations, not only the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"After the main body, flush floats, place references, then clear the page and use appendix plus a Supplementary Information section with substantive subsections. Add a separate LLM Usage section, preferably there, disclosing the documented roles in ideation, code preparation and paper planning/writing without inventing model identifiers or human review. Follow any supplied authoritative appendix rankings later without retroactively changing this strategy or hiding central evidence.\\\",\n+    \\\"This is a framing artifact only. Do not create paper.tex or claims_grounding.json here, do not run final-paper validation, and do not claim official-template provenance or submission readiness merely because the supplied local style was inspected. Downstream writing must retain venue anonymization, actual checklist obligations, figure/script traceability, and all evaluation limitations.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Strategy: Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability\n+\n+## Decision\n+\n+**Status: ready.** Use the \"'`paper_standalone` family and `write-paper-standalone` skill for a thesis-first ICLR 2026 study. Provisional title: **Fixed-Game SHAP Reliability: Structure, Budgets, and Reference Limits**.\n+\n+**Central question.** For frozen tabular classifiers and a fixed empirical probability-scale Shapley game, how do sampled and structure-aware computations compare in single-call reference agreement and repeated-call consistency under finite coalition caps, and what reliability claims remain unsupported?\n+\n+**Central thesis.** On the evaluated German Credit and ACS income conditions, structure-aware forest attribution and probability-scale logistic integration yield perfectly consistent observed repeated-call top-three sets and signs and high reference agreement, but reference uncertainty, restricted game semantics, and unequal computational access prevent interpreting these results as general deployment reliability or equal-time superiority.\n+\n+This is one shared scientific question with dataset/model-specific adaptations, not separate chronological experiments. The contribution is a bounded computational-reliability comparison and its interpretive limits, not a first-ever exact-tree algorithm, universal reliability theorem, or deployment certification.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification\n+\n+Read final evaluation independently of search and of any proposed downstream-study narrative. Here `paper_data.json.downstream_study` and `study.*` sources are absent. The final qualification sources report:\n+\n+| Grounding source | Reported value |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| `final.qualification.status` | `completed` |\n+| `final.qualification.outcome` | `qualified` |\n+| `final.qualification.correct` | `true` |\n+\n+No failed final qualification is reported in this run. This outcome concerns the documented evaluation checks, not proof that explanations are valid reasons for high-risk decisions. Preserve the distinction in writing, review, audit, and revision. If later authoritative evidence reports failure, disclose it and retain its limitations; do not classify its cause as performance, validity, or adaptivity without evaluator diagnostics.\n+\n+Main numerical evidence comes from `final.evidence.episodes`. Final aggregates include reference agreement **0.9975639445869278**, reference top-three overlap **1.0**, and all-coordinate sign agreement **0.9997395833333332**, grounded in their corresponding `final.metric.*` sources. Candidate repeat-pair top-three and sign agreement are **1.0** throughout the retained final empirical observations. These are separate findings, not one undifferentiated reliability score. Controls, efficiency, failed-call fraction and replay are narrow checks.\n+\n+The final wall total, **700.3707705293782 seconds**, covers the evaluation workload, including references and comparators; it is not per-explanation latency or a candidate-only runtime. The source brief'\"'s CPU-hour estimate is not measured usage.\n+\n+### What is actually evaluated\n+\n+- German Credit and **ACSIncome-2024-RELSHIPP**, each with logistic regression and random forests: four conditions under one thesis.\n+- Final episode seeds: **104729, 130363, 155921**; coalition caps **64, 256, 1024**; **six** candidate calls per cap; **16** fixed query instances and **16** fixed training-background rows per condition.\n+- German has **20** scalar feature groups and retained final splits **300/100/100** for training/validation/explanation. ACS has **10** groups and **20000/6667/6667**. Split counts are inspected resource provenance, not generalization measurements.\n+- Preprocessing is training-fitted ordinal categorical encoding, numeric median imputation, and standardization of supplied original groups. This is not arbitrary raw-data masking or a one-hot-grouping experiment.\n+- Logistic regression uses \"'`lbfgs`, `max_iter=500`, `tol=1e-7`; forests have **64** trees, maximum depth **6**, and `n_jobs=1`.\n+- ACS references enumerate the finite **10**-feature game. German references average two **4096**-coalition library estimates; their half-difference is a recorded disagreement proxy, not a confidence interval or exact ground truth.\n+\n+These settings are traceable to the final episode arrays, `task/evaluate_final.py`, and `task/resources/final/`. The ACS relationship-field adapter and search/final predictor-content separation must remain explicit. Do not call the adapted task bit-identical historical ACSIncome.\n+\n+## Framing Choice and Alternatives\n+\n+**Story status: recentered.** There is no prior manuscript, edit-context file, `previous_paper/`, `aggregated/`, or `extra_tasks/` directory. This decision narrows the broad source-task motivation rather than modifying an unseen prior paper.\n+\n+| Candidate story | Decision and grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Preserve the broad claim about reliable reasons in high-risk deployment | Reject: no human decision evidence, causal validation, conditional-game study, or background-shift evaluation. |\n+| Shared fixed-game computation across model families | Select: both forest and logistic conditions have measured comparators and reference evidence, with inspectable component changes. |\n+| Recenter solely on logistic quadrature | Reject as primary: discards useful forest evidence; no recorded branch coverage or total quadrature-error certificate supports making quadrature alone the whole claim. |\n+| Center single-call confidence certificates | Reject: certificate decisions and acceptance coverage were not persisted; implementation presence is not measured utility. |\n+| Narrate the selected search result | Reject: discovery order and selection scores do not answer the scientific question or establish final performance. |\n+\n+The recoverable full implementation is under `results/ideas/03_probability_scale_logistic_shap_by_bounded_fourier_quadrature/program_1/src/`. The best-program manifest links this configuration to the final-tested method at selection/path level; the final program-tree digest is recorded but has not independently been matched to a recovered byte-identical final snapshot in this stage. Describe source-grounded mechanisms and evidence-grounded behavior separately.\n+\n+Private-only selection context must not leak into manuscript labels. Without `study.*`, do not manufacture a frozen-study selection contract, publish search score differences or attempt totals, or use the memory-only original-incumbent score as a comparison. The stored library comparators remain valid measured baselines.\n+\n+## Methods Worth Including\n+\n+1. **One-shot library Kernel SHAP — baseline.** Same model, empirical background, queries, identity link and nominal cap; `l1_reg=0.0`.\n+2. **Two-start split-cap Kernel SHAP — baseline.** Average two independent half-cap estimates. Explain that endpoint overhead and actual prediction rows need not match one-shot cost.\n+3. **Structure-aware fixed-game computation — proposed family.** Exact forest leaf-literal algebra and probability-scale logistic Fourier/Owen integration, with exhaustive nonforest dispatch when all subsets fit and the existing sampled fallback on numerical rejection. Explain the common estimand before model-specific computations.\n+4. **Sampled path/regression configuration — development ablation.** Compared with the forest-enabled configuration on forest conditions; not the untouched original incumbent.\n+5. **Forest-enabled, sampled-logistic configuration — development ablation.** Compared with the full family on logistic conditions; unchanged forest behavior checks component locality.\n+6. **Same-game references and analytic controls — supporting evidence.** Exhaustive ACS, approximate German, zero/affine/permutation controls, and reset/replay. Do not count them as extra public datasets or as full nonlinear validation.\n+\n+Inspection of `reliability.py` confirms that the forest comparison adds its import/dispatch and the logistic comparison adds its import/dispatch. Stored matched development episodes support direct component contrasts at seeds **1729/2718** and caps **64/256**. Label these comparisons development data throughout; they are neither final holdout ablations nor independent confirmations. Complete tables may go in the supplement, but the main component comparison must remain visible.\n+\n+Do not expand the paper into unmeasured neural models, background resampling, alternative certificates, leverage-score methods, external TreeSHAP implementations, or additional datasets. Relevant literature methods may be context, not measured baselines.\n+\n+## Results Organization and Statistical Meaning\n+\n+### Main final comparison\n+\n+Compare three methods at each cap in each dataset/model condition. Use normalized L1 **reference agreement**:\n+\n+`1 / (1 + ||phi - phi_ref||_1 / max(||phi_ref||_1, 0.001))`.\n+\n+Show individual episode markers rather than invented per-cap confidence bands. Preserve the distinction between approximate German and exhaustive ACS references. High-cap ACS one-shot computation can close the gap; split-cap averaging has particularly poor German agreement at cap 64. Report these negative and boundary results without an unsupported diagnosis such as regression rank failure.\n+\n+### Distinct reliability assessments\n+\n+- Reference top-three overlap uses absolute values and original-column tie breaking.\n+- Reference sign agreement covers **all coordinates**, with absolute zero tolerance **1e-8**; it is not signed-top-three accuracy.\n+- Repeated-call top-three and sign agreement compare candidate outputs on the same fixed game. Baseline outputs do not include six within-model repetitions, so a matching baseline repeatability comparison is unavailable.\n+- Normalized efficiency residual uses a **0.001** denominator floor and is capped at one. It is not reference fidelity.\n+\n+Existing case-level 95% bootstrap intervals first average candidate agreement over repetitions and caps and then resample **16 instances**, using **1000** bootstrap draws and seed **84017**. They condition on a fitted model and its reference; they are not per-cap intervals and omit reference-estimation uncertainty. Do not average interval endpoints into a new interval. The same instances recur across episodes, and fitted forests may differ with seeds; neither repeated calls nor overlapping episode samples create independent people. Near-degenerate intervals from deterministic outputs do not imply negligible deployment uncertainty.\n+\n+### Limits required beside the main results\n+\n+Residual German differences cannot be assigned solely to reference noise or solely to candidate error. Deterministic outputs cannot establish the active internal branch. Nonforest exhaustive dispatch occurs at cap `>= 2''^d - 2`; ACS logistic cap 1024 is therefore not evidence of the quadrature branch. Internal certificate acceptance/rejection, quadrature rejection frequency, candidate per-call runtime, and total discretization-error guarantees are unavailable.\n+\n+The proposed family has model-parameter access; library methods use prediction queries. A nominal sampled-coalition cap does not equate arithmetic work, information access, or wall time. Do not claim equal-time superiority. The quadrature'\"'s analytic frequency-tail bound does not bound all discretization error; refinement agreement and efficiency are numerical diagnostics. Independent validation scripts are present but their preparation records say they were not run. Their presence cannot become a validation result.\n+\n+No acceptable-error or user-decision reliability threshold was prespecified. State that one call meets the **observed same-game criteria in these retained conditions**, not that a universal trustworthy-explanation threshold was established.\n+\n+## Figure Specifications and Layout\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`article` and `paper,times`; `paper.sty` sets **5.5 inches text width**, **9 inches text height**, and a **single-column** layout. Full width means that one text column, not a two-column float. Half-width placement is not appropriate for the required composites.\n+\n+### Figure 1 — `fixed_game_overview`\n+\n+- **Required; diagram; generator `generate-concept-figure`.** Early placement on page 1 or 2.\n+- One panel with at most six concise blocks: fixed game, sampled computation, structure-aware computation, repeat consistency, reference agreement, and scope boundary. Explain details in the caption rather than adding microtext.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **1.6–1.8 inches** high plus caption; intended footprint about **0.23 page**. At least **9-point** final-size text.\n+- Budget: **1 panel**, **1 per row**, **6 main categories/blocks**, **2 computational branches**. No invented numeric annotations or causal/deployment guarantees.\n+- Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes` plus the inspected estimator source. This is an evidence map, not a claim that a confidence certificate was observed.\n+- Use the orchestrator-owned editable draw.io concept-figure workflow later; do not run it during strategy planning. At most this one overview uses that generator.\n+\n+### Figure 2 — `final_reference_comparison`\n+\n+- **Required; grouped categorical dot plot; matplotlib.** Four dataset/model panels in a **2x2** arrangement.\n+- Three cap categories and three method series per panel; per-episode points, one shared legend, explicit exhaustive/approximate reference labels. A common **0–1** agreement scale keeps the low split-cap outcomes visible; communicate near-ceiling differences through concise values or the companion table, not a hidden truncated scale.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **3.5–4 inches** high plus caption; footprint about **0.48 page**. Roughly **2.6 inches** per panel supports short cap labels and at least **9-point** text.\n+- Budget: **4 panels**, **2 per row**, **3 categories**, **3 series**. No search-order lines or per-cap error bars borrowed from budget-pooled intervals.\n+- Grounding: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.reference_fidelity`.\n+\n+### Figure 3 — `component_comparison`\n+\n+- **Required; paired categorical dot comparison; matplotlib.** Two panels: forest component and logistic component.\n+- Four dataset/cap categories per panel, two compared configurations, and the two matched development episode points. Show the relevant disabled/enabled contrast rather than all configurations in an ordered sequence.\n+- Full **5.5-inch** width, approximately **2.2–2.5 inches** high plus caption; footprint about **0.32 page**. Short labels and at least **9-point** text are required; simplify instead of shrinking.\n+- Budget: **2 panels**, **2 per row**, **4 categories**, **2 series**. Explicitly mark development data. No campaign progression, ranking, or final-set ablation claim.\n+- Private grounding bridge: `result.top_program_03` identifies sampled-only, `result.top_program_02` forest-enabled, and `result.top_program_01` full computation. Use their actual `all_programs[*].evaluation_evidence.episodes` arrays and inspected source changes, not the scalar selection scores, as evidence for the plotted component contrasts.\n+\n+### Export and consistency contract\n+\n+Quantitative figures must retain source/data and export **PDF plus PNG**, PNG at **300 DPI**. LaTeX must use the PDF whenever available. For raster-only full-width assets, regenerate at **at least 2400 pixels wide**; column/partial-width raster assets require **at least 1200 pixels**. Never upscale an existing raster. The concept workflow does not itself promise a PDF: prefer one exported from its editable vector source when available, otherwise meet the raster minimum and preserve the prompt/source manifest.\n+\n+Use gray for one-shot library, orange for split-cap averaging, and blue for structure-aware computation. Component plots may use gray/blue for the explicitly labeled disabled/enabled contrast. Keep reference quality as text labels, not a remapping of method colors. No trajectory figures are warranted.\n+\n+## Body Budget and Reader Value\n+\n+Target **8.5 body pages** under the supplied **8–9-page** brief. Figures and tables are already included in these allocations:\n+\n+| Material | Planned pages |\n+| --- | ---: |\n+| Introduction and early overview | 1.25 |\n+| Related work | 0.65 |\n+| Fixed-game estimand and metrics | 1.00 |\n+| Model-specific computation | 1.40 |\n+| Experimental and statistical protocol | 1.05 |\n+| Results and component comparison | 2.00 |\n+| Limitations and interpretation | 0.90 |\n+| Conclusion | 0.25 |\n+\n+Keep two compact main tables: experimental geometry and condition-specific final reliability. The latter can present the existing conditional intervals at their true scope, alongside separate repeat consistency, reference top-three/sign agreement, and a nearby integrity-check paragraph. Do not force all diagnostics into an unreadable table.\n+\n+Spend available space on the common game definition, the nonlinear probability-scale mechanism, independent meaning of metrics, reference limitations, and fair-compute discussion. Do not pad with method history, oversized graphics, redundant tables, untested possibilities, or search scores. If ending at eight pages, its last page must be at least 75% filled; do not alter margins or shrink type to manipulate this. The supplied template'\"'s sample final-copy author block is not suitable for double-blind submission.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Flush main floats, place references, then clear the page, enter appendix mode, and add **Supplementary Information**. The following substantive sections use available evidence; they do not require new experiments or guessed posthoc rankings:\n+\n+1. **Fixed-Game Definition and Preprocessing.** Expand the estimand, original-group representation, training-only preprocessing, exact data/split provenance and ACS adapter. Sources: \"'`final.evidence.episodes` with inspected `task/evaluate_final.py` and final resource records.\n+2. **Structure-Aware Computation and Numerical Safeguards.** Include leaf inclusion/exclusion coefficients, repeated splits and float semantics, Fourier/Owen integration, inclusion quadrature, frequency-tail versus discretization distinction, dispatch and fallback. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `result.top_program_01`, and the recoverable estimator files; label unrun validation scripts accurately.\n+3. **Episode-Level Reliability and Reference Uncertainty.** Complete per-case/cap/episode tables, stored bootstrap intervals at their actual scope, reference half-differences, model diagnostics, controls and replay. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes` and `final.metric.efficiency_error`, `final.metric.control_pass_rate`, `final.metric.replay_error`, `final.metric.failed_fraction`.\n+4. **Component Comparison Details.** Full development comparison tables, source dispatch differences, unchanged-family checks, and recorded regressions/nonmonotone cap behavior. Sources: `result.top_program_01`, `result.top_program_02`, `result.top_program_03` followed to their episode arrays. No selection-score narrative or final-confirmation claim.\n+5. **Reproducibility and Compute Accounting.** Dependencies, program specifications, seeds, offline data acquisition/provenance, hashes, commands, measured timing scopes, and exact figure/table script mapping once implemented. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.wall_seconds`, and the three final qualification sources, with inspected local specifications/resources. No identifying internal paths in the anonymous submission.\n+\n+Add a separate **LLM Usage** section, preferably after these appendix subsections, describing documented ideation, code-preparation, framing and writing roles precisely. Do not invent model identifiers, human verification, or independent execution. Follow later authoritative appendix rankings without retroactively rewriting this strategy; never move essential final evidence or decisive limitations out of the body.\n+\n+## Literature, Access, and Disclosure Boundaries\n+\n+The existing bibliography is a noisy retrieved candidate pool with metadata-level provenance. It is not evidence that every source was read. Start only with relevant permitted primary records such as `Lundberg2017AUA`, `Musco2024ProvablyAS`, and appropriate tree-attribution records after actual source verification. Do not use irrelevant retrievals as citation padding, invent missing Owen/empirical-Bernstein/semantic references, or claim unverified theoretical novelty. Nonessential certificate theory should not carry the central thesis.\n+\n+No external paper pages were accessed in this strategy stage and no prohibited encounter was identified here. This does not certify earlier retrieval as reviewed or contamination-free. Do not attempt to identify the prohibited study or conduct broad rerun-reliability discovery. Stop and record any actual forbidden encounter, including where it occurred and how much was read.\n+\n+## Anti-Diary and Overclaim Guardrails\n+\n+Avoid headings **Search Progression**, **Campaign Phases**, **Milestones**, **First Valid Result**, **Iteration History**, **Experiment A / Experiment B**, **Winning Configuration**, and **Successive Improvements**.\n+\n+Forbidden visible wording includes “we then tried,” “subsequent improvements,” “first valid result,” “next-best,” “later variants,” and the internal labels listed in the JSON contract. Also avoid “state of the art,” “certified reliable explanations,” “repeatability proves validity,” “exact German ground truth,” “equal-time superiority,” and “safe high-risk deployment.” Private-only source identifiers in this memo are not recommended manuscript terminology.\n+\n+Never turn unscored or unrun alternatives into measured losses. Never invent significance, certificate coverage, quadrature branch counts, candidate latency, robustness studies, additional datasets or external-baseline experiments. Retain the fixed small query set, fixed background, scalar encoding, approximate German reference, missing branch diagnostics, and absent human/causal/background-shift validation in the main limitations.\n+\n+This stage produces strategy only: no `paper.tex`, no `claims_grounding.json`, no final-paper validation, and no claim of submission readiness or verified official-template provenance merely from inspecting the supplied local style.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA paper_strategy.json\nA paper_strategy.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
